---
title: "Care of Maternal, Newborn, and Pediatric Patients"
code: "PNE-136"
category: "practical-nursing"
credits: "4"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Uses a family-centered approach; studies normal and common complications in pregnancy, childbirth, post-partum, the neonate, and children through adolescence. Covers milestones in all aspects of growth and development and common childhood disorders at various ages. Lecture 4 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
